  "limits": [
    "The independent C oracle extracts unchanged released G_DoCompleted/G_WorldDone and WI single-player counter/input functions. Unrelated music, graphics and multiplayer callbacks are stubbed; those behaviors are not proved here.",
    "212 route/history cases cover all episodic maps, normal Phase 2 routes and the authored MAP15/MAP31 secret routes. Thirty-six invalid map or unsupported commercial secret-route calls throw.",
    "144 scenarios compare 92,160 tick records including percentage/time/par values, held and newly pressed attack/use bits, effect sound order and completion phase. Native task heap returns to its original usage.",
    "The released episode-four par lookup reads outside its array. The routing oracle supplies a safe dummy row and does not compare par time. The native component takes an explicit par value with zero default; authored metadata loading remains separate.",
    "Official Freedoom 0.13.0 Phase 1 secret exits occur in E1M3/E2M5/E3M6/E4M2. Phase 2 secret exits occur only in MAP15/MAP31. Unsupported Phase 2 secret routes are rejected rather than carrying a stale target.",
    "TmIntermission is outside Load/Run. Current Play still shows LEVEL COMPLETE; actual next-map ownership, intermission rendering, persistent secret tracking, authored metadata, music and finale UI are unfinished.",
    "These checks establish native and frozen-HEMU component behavior. They do not establish full gameplay, performance, every CPU architecture or bare-metal compatibility."
